    { "type": "h1", "text": "1. Greetings and polite words" },
    {
      "type": "verbpairs",
      "title": "Greetings and politeness",
      "widths": [4.6, 3.9, 4.6, 3.9],
      "items": [
        ["hola", "hello"], ["buenos días", "good morning"], ["buenas tardes", "good afternoon"], ["buenas noches", "good evening, good night"],
        ["adiós", "goodbye"], ["hasta luego", "see you later"], ["hasta mañana", "see you tomorrow"], ["hasta pronto", "see you soon"],
        ["por favor", "please"], ["gracias", "thank you"], ["de nada", "you are welcome"], ["perdón", "sorry, excuse me"],
        ["lo siento", "I am sorry"], ["con permiso", "excuse me (passing)"], ["¿qué tal?", "how is it going?"], ["¿cómo estás?", "how are you?"],
        ["(muy) bien", "(very) well"], ["así así", "so-so"], ["mal", "bad"], ["mucho gusto", "nice to meet you"],
        ["encantado / encantada", "pleased to meet you"], ["sí / no", "yes / no"], ["vale", "OK (very common in Spain)"], ["bienvenido / bienvenida", "welcome"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "spain",
      "title": "Which greeting when?",
      "text": "Lunch in Spain is around 2 pm, so <b>buenos días</b> is used until about then. <b>Buenas tardes</b> lasts until it gets dark, then it is <b>buenas noches</b>, also as a way of saying goodnight."
    },

    { "type": "h1", "text": "2. Numbers" },
    {
      "type": "verbpairs",
      "title": "Numbers",
      "items": [
        ["0", "cero"], ["1", "uno"], ["2", "dos"], ["3", "tres"], ["4", "cuatro"], ["5", "cinco"], ["6", "seis"], ["7", "siete"],
        ["8", "ocho"], ["9", "nueve"], ["10", "diez"], ["11", "once"], ["12", "doce"], ["13", "trece"], ["14", "catorce"], ["15", "quince"],
        ["16", "dieciséis"], ["17", "diecisiete"], ["18", "dieciocho"], ["19", "diecinueve"], ["20", "veinte"], ["30", "treinta"], ["40", "cuarenta"], ["50", "cincuenta"],
        ["60", "sesenta"], ["70", "setenta"], ["80", "ochenta"], ["90", "noventa"], ["100", "cien"], ["200", "doscientos"], ["500", "quinientos"], ["1000", "mil"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "<b>16 to 19 and 21 to 29</b> are one word: dieciséis, diecisiete, veintiuno, veintidós, veintitrés, veinticuatro, veinticinco, veintiséis, veintisiete, veintiocho, veintinueve.",
        "<b>From 31</b> the tens and units are separate words with y: treinta y uno, cuarenta y cinco, noventa y nueve.",
        "<b>100:</b> <i>cien</i> on its own or before a noun (cien euros), <i>ciento</i> in 101 to 199 (ciento uno, ciento cincuenta).",
        "<b>uno</b> shortens before a masculine noun and agrees with a feminine one: <i>un euro, veintiún euros, una casa, veintiuna casas</i>. Hundreds agree too: <i>doscientas casas</i>.",
        "<b>mil</b> never takes un: <i>mil euros</i>."
      ]
    },

