    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Days and months are written in lower case. The week starts on Monday. <i>El lunes</i> = on Monday, <i>los lunes</i> = on Mondays. Dates use cardinal numbers: <i>el cinco de mayo</i>, <i>el 1 de enero</i>. Seasons: <i>en verano</i>, <i>en invierno</i>."
    },

    { "type": "h1", "text": "4. Telling the time" },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [2.6, 7.4, 7.0],
      "head": ["Time", "Spanish", "English"],
      "rows": [
        ["1:00", "Es la una.", "It is one o'clock."],
        ["2:00", "Son las dos.", "It is two o'clock."],
        ["2:15", "Son las dos y cuarto.", "It is a quarter past two."],
        ["2:30", "Son las dos y media.", "It is half past two."],
        ["2:45", "Son las tres menos cuarto.", "It is a quarter to three."],
        ["2:10", "Son las dos y diez.", "It is ten past two."],
        ["2:50", "Son las tres menos diez.", "It is ten to three."],
        ["12:00", "Es mediodía.", "It is noon."],
        ["0:00", "Es medianoche.", "It is midnight."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "<b>¿Qué hora es?</b> (What time is it?) <b>¿A qué hora…?</b> (At what time…?) Answer: <i>A las ocho.</i>",
        "Use <b>es la</b> for one o'clock and <b>son las</b> for every other hour.",
        "Add <b>de la mañana</b> (morning), <b>de la tarde</b> (afternoon and evening) or <b>de la noche</b> (night): <i>las ocho de la mañana, las diez de la noche</i>."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "dutch",
      "title": "Half drie is not “media tres”",
      "text": "Dutch <i>half drie</i> means 2:30, and so does Spanish <b>las dos y media</b>. Do not translate <i>half drie</i> word for word. Spanish adds the half <b>after</b> the hour that has already started."
    },

