      "widths": [4.6, 6.0, 6.4],
      "head": ["Spain", "Latin America (common)", "English"],
      "rows": [
        ["el coche", "el carro, el auto", "car"],
        ["el ordenador", "la computadora", "computer"],
        ["el móvil", "el celular", "mobile phone"],
        ["el zumo", "el jugo", "juice"],
        ["la patata", "la papa", "potato"],
        ["el piso", "el apartamento, el departamento", "flat"],
        ["las gafas", "los lentes, los anteojos", "glasses"],
        ["el billete", "el boleto, el pasaje", "ticket"],
        ["conducir, aparcar", "manejar, estacionar", "to drive, to park"],
        ["vosotros", "ustedes", "you (plural, informal)"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "latam_ok": true,
      "items": [
        "Careful with <b>coger</b>: in Spain it is the normal verb for taking a bus (<i>coger el autobús</i>), but in parts of Latin America it has a vulgar meaning. There people say <i>tomar</i>.",
        "Pronunciation also differs: Spain says <i>c</i> and <i>z</i> as th (<i>gracias</i>), Latin America as s."
      ]
    },

